WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.420
As the entertainment world reels from the
death of Matthew Perry, some of his "Friends"

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.470
co-stars have taken to social media to share
their touching tributes.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:14.800
From guest stars like Morgan Fairchild to
the main cast, here's what they had to say.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.550
On "Friends," Maggie Wheeler played Chandler's
on-again-off-again girlfriend, Janice.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:24.230
Off-camera, Wheeler and Perry were pals, and
she was among the first to pay tribute to

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.720
him on social media.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:26.900
She wrote on Instagram:

00:00:27.438 --> 00:00:28.380
"What a loss.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.780
The world will miss you Mathew Perry.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.690
The joy you brought to so many in your too
short lifetime will live on.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:39.040
I feel so very blessed by every creative moment
we shared."

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.719
Morgan Fairchild, who played Chandler's complicated
mother Nora throughout the run of "Friends,"

00:00:43.719 --> 00:00:48.040
acknowledged Matthew Perry's death on X, formerly
known as Twitter, writing,

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.520
"I'm heartbroken about the untimely death
of my 'son', Matthew Perry.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.510
The loss of such a brilliant young actor is
a shock."

00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:00.090
Fairchild went on to offer her thoughts specifically
to John Bennett Perry, his father.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:06.730
The elder Perry worked together with Fairchild
on the 1980s soap operas "Flamingo Road" and "Falcon Crest."

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:11.840
John Bennett Perry also appeared on "Friends"
as Mr. Burgin in a Season 4 episode.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.619
It also seems as if the two shared a close
father-son relationship, as Matthew posted

00:01:16.619 --> 00:01:19.780
a picture of them together on Instagram recently.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:24.229
Selma Blair paid tribute to Matthew Perry
on her Instagram, where she affectionately

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:29.310
referred to her one-time "Friends" co-star
as her "oldest boy friend." Blair wrote,

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:32.367
"All of us loved Matthew, and I did especially.

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:33.367
Every day.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:34.587
I loved him unconditionally.

00:01:34.724 --> 00:01:35.724
And he me.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:36.989
And I'm broken.

00:01:37.103 --> 00:01:38.253
Broke hearted.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:39.371
Sweet dreams, Matty.

00:01:39.371 --> 00:01:40.650
Sweet dreams."

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:46.630
Blair played Chandler's flirtatious co-worker
Wendy in the episode "The One With Christmas in Tulsa."

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:51.350
It was a memorable role that unfortunately
didn't recur throughout the series.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:56.100
Another famous Chandler ex-girlfriend on "Friends"
was Kathy, played by Paget Brewster, who hung

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.310
out with the group during Season 4.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:02.579
Originally introduced as a new girlfriend
for Joey, Chandler finds himself falling in

00:02:02.579 --> 00:02:07.341
love with her despite all his efforts, eventually
culminating in a scene where she gives him

00:02:07.341 --> 00:02:08.770
a haircut and they kiss.

00:02:09.457 --> 00:02:10.330
"Did you sleep with her?"

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.268
"No, no, no, I just kissed her."

00:02:12.268 --> 00:02:13.062
"What?!

00:02:13.062 --> 00:02:14.062
That's even worse."

00:02:14.165 --> 00:02:19.150
This incident nearly destroys the iconic bromance
between the two roommates, which is only resolved

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:23.350
after Joey makes Chandler sit in a wooden
box and think about what he's done.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:27.440
Following this, with Joey's blessing, Kathy
and Chandler briefly date.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.349
However, their relationship doesn't work out
in the end.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:34.240
Brewster also shared her response to the tragic
loss of Matthew Perry.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:38.500
In a post to her X account, she shared warm
memories of the actor, writing,

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:41.770
"I'm so very sad to hear about @MatthewPerry.

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:46.150
He was lovely to me on Friends and every time
I saw him in the decades after.

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.590
Please read his book.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.184
It was his legacy to help.

00:02:49.184 --> 00:02:50.795
He won't rest in peace though..

00:02:50.795 --> 00:02:54.110
He's already too busy making everyone laugh
up there."

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:57.930
Two days after news of Matthew Perry's death
came to light, the remaining cast members

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:01.390
of "Friends" came together to honor their
friend and co-star.

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:02.940
They wrote in their statement to People,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:06.463
"We are all so utterly devastated by the loss
of Matthew.

00:03:06.463 --> 00:03:08.260
We were more than just cast mates.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.390
We are a family."

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:13.900
They added that they are taking time to process
the loss of Perry, and they will have more

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.680
to say in the near future.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.604
The actors concluded by writing,

00:03:17.604 --> 00:03:22.269
"For now, our thoughts and our love are with
Matty's family, his friends, and everyone

00:03:22.269 --> 00:03:23.910
who loved him around the world."

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:29.049
Their statement came one day after "Friends"
creators Marta Kauffman and David Crane, as

00:03:29.049 --> 00:03:33.385
well as executive producer Kevin Bright, released
a joint statement of their own.

00:03:33.385 --> 00:03:34.610
Their statement said:

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:39.681
"We will always cherish the joy, the light,
the blinding intelligence he brought to every

00:03:39.681 --> 00:03:43.459
moment — not just to his work, but in life
as well."

00:03:43.459 --> 00:03:48.170
They also recalled that from the very beginning,
they felt Perry was the absolute perfect fit

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:49.703
for the role of Chandler Bing.

00:03:49.863 --> 00:03:52.078
To say they were right would be an understatement.

